{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014KnhxMi3mfnSZjQ1v32XJ5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Plan: Epic 7 Archive and Derived Views\n2\t\n3\t## Purpose\n4\t\n5\tThis test plan maps every Epic 7 test condition to planned tests. It verifies\n6\tcanonical archive append/read behavior, finalization boundaries, archive read\n7\tsurfaces, turn derivation, structural derived views, provenance enrichment, and\n8\tdegraded reads.\n9\t\n10\tRelated design: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md`\n11\t\n12\t## Test Strategy\n13\t\n14\t### Test Layers\n15\t\n16\t| Layer | Files | Purpose |\n17\t|-------|-------|---------|\n18\t| Convex service tests | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts`, `convex/archiveTurns.test.ts`, `convex/derivedArchiveViews.test.ts` | Durable append/read, sequence, idempotency, cached projections |\n19\t| Fastify service/API tests | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | Auth/access, finalization policy, archive reads, derivation, degraded states |\n20\t| Client service tests | `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts`, `tests/service/client/archive-turns-section.test.ts`, `tests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts` | User-visible archive, turn, structural-view, empty, pagination, and degraded states |\n21\t| Existing live/process tests | `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/process-execution-orchestrator.test.ts` | Ensure live upserts remain separate from archive finalization |\n22\t\n23\t### Scope Boundaries\n24\t\n25\t| Story | Owns | Does Not Prove |\n26\t|-------|------|----------------|\n27\t| 1 Archive persistence | Convex archive-entry primitive, taxonomy, sequence ordering, idempotency guard, related-id round-trip | Service finalization hooks, archive route/UI, read-time artifact/source enrichment |\n28\t| 2 Finalization boundary | Service-level proof that completed live objects append exactly once and partial/delta objects do not append | Primitive storage mechanics beyond Story 1 contract, browser archive read surface |\n29\t| 3 Archive read/reopen | Authenticated route/UI, reload/environment-loss reads, access checks, bounded page contract, displaying degraded entries already present in the response | Deep artifact/source provenance enrichment or lookup-failure degradation semantics |\n30\t| 6 Provenance coherence | Artifact/source enrichment and per-entry lookup-failure degradation semantics | Replacing Story 3 route/UI, access, reload, or bounded-page behavior |\n31\t\n32\t### Mock Boundaries\n33\t\n34\t| Boundary | Mock? | Notes |\n35\t|----------|-------|-------|\n36\t| Artifact/source enrichment services | Yes in Story 6 archive read tests | Mock unavailable related context to verify per-entry degradation |\n37\t| Environment/provider runtime | Yes | Finalization tests use completed/interrupted fake runtime objects |\n38\t| Convex in route tests | Existing fake/in-memory PlatformStore pattern | Route tests exercise Fastify services without live Convex |\n39\t| Internal derivation helpers | No | Test via `TurnDerivationService` and `DerivedArchiveViewService` |\n40\t| Client API calls | Yes | Client tests mock fetch/API layer only |\n41\t\n42\t## TC to Test Mapping\n43\t\n44\t| TC | Test File | Test Description | Coverage Notes |\n45\t|----|-----------|------------------|----------------|\n46\t| TC-1.1a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.1a appends finalized user_message entry through primitive` | Trusted caller payload persists as canonical `user_message` row |\n47\t| TC-1.1b | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.1b appends finalized model_message entry through primitive` | Trusted caller payload persists as canonical `model_message` row |\n48\t| TC-1.1c | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.1c appends finalized process_event entry through primitive` | Trusted caller payload persists as canonical `process_event` row |\n49\t| TC-1.2a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.2a accepts required archive entry kinds` | All seven kinds accepted |\n50\t| TC-1.2b | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.2b rejects unsupported archive entry kind` | Invalid kind creates no row |\n51\t| TC-1.3a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.3a reads entries in stable sequence order` | Ascending sequence |\n52\t| TC-1.3b | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.3b same timestamp entries remain deterministic` | Sequence breaks timestamp ties |\n53\t| TC-1.4a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.4a round-trips related ids on archive row` | Related artifact/source/tool ids return unchanged from canonical row |\n54\t| TC-1.4b | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.4b archive row remains readable without related-record lookup` | Primitive read does not require enrichment |\n55\t| TC-2.1a | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `TC-2.1a raw streaming delta excluded from archive` | Delta object never calls append |\n56\t| TC-2.2a | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `TC-2.2a interrupted model output excluded` | Interrupted object ignored |\n57\t| TC-2.2b | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `TC-2.2b incomplete tool result excluded` | Tool result without finalization ignored |\n58\t| TC-2.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `TC-2.3a completed live object archived once through finalization service` | Finalization service appends one canonical entry |\n59\t| TC-2.3b | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `TC-2.3b replayed completion does not duplicate entry through service boundary` | Retried completion does not duplicate archive append |\n60\t| TC-3.1a | `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts` | `TC-3.1a archive entries visible` | Client renders finalized entries |\n61\t| TC-3.1b | `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts` | `TC-3.1b empty archive state visible` | Empty state rendered |\n62\t| TC-3.2a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-3.2a archive survives reload` | GET archive reads durable state |\n63\t| TC-3.2b | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-3.2b archive survives environment loss` | Environment absent does not affect archive read |\n64\t| TC-3.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-3.3a unauthorized archive read blocked` | 403/401 without leakage |\n65\t| TC-3.3b | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-3.3b missing process archive read returns not found` | 404 `PROCESS_NOT_FOUND` |\n66\t| TC-3.4a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-3.4a degraded entry displayed with healthy entries` | Mixed ready/degraded page without hiding healthy rows |\n67\t| TC-4.1a | `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | `TC-4.1a turns derived from archive` | Entries grouped into turns |\n68\t| TC-4.1b | `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | `TC-4.1b empty archive produces empty turn view` | Empty turns response |\n69\t| TC-4.2a | `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | `TC-4.2a turn includes archive entry references` | Turn carries source entry ids |\n70\t| TC-4.3a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-4.3a archive unchanged after turn derivation` | Entry rows unchanged after rebuild |\n71\t| TC-4.4a | `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | `TC-4.4a degraded turn returned` | One degraded turn does not hide others |\n72\t| TC-5.1a | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-5.1a derived view returned for turn range` | `turn_range` view returned without summary text |\n73\t| TC-5.2a | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-5.2a derived view identifies boundary` | start/end turn indexes and entry refs |\n74\t| TC-5.3a | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-5.3a derived view references source turns` | Source turn ids present |\n75\t| TC-5.3b | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-5.3b derived view can trace to archive entries` | Source archive ids present |\n76\t| TC-5.4a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-5.4a archive remains after derived view creation` | Archive rows still readable |\n77\t| TC-5.5a | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-5.5a derived view failure leaves archive readable` | Archive read succeeds after failed refresh |\n78\t| TC-5.5b | `tests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts` | `TC-5.5b derived view reports degraded status` | Client renders degraded view |\n79\t| TC-6.1a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.1a artifact provenance visible from archive entry` | Artifact version context visible |\n80\t| TC-6.2a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.2a source provenance visible from archive entry` | Repository identity/ref visible |\n81\t| TC-6.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.3a missing source context degrades one entry` | Entry visible with degraded source context |\n82\t| TC-6.3b | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.3b missing artifact context degrades one entry` | Entry visible with degraded artifact context |\n83\t| TC-7.1a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-7.1a archive and turn reads restore after reload` | Durable archive and cached/rebuilt turns readable |\n84\t| TC-7.1b | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-7.1b derived view restores after reload` | View readable or rebuilt |\n85\t| TC-7.2a | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-7.2a canonical archive remains visible during derived-view failure` | Archive unaffected by view failure |\n86\t| TC-7.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-7.3a archive read returns bounded page` | Page has limit and next cursor |\n87\t\n88\t## Non-TC Decided Tests\n89\t\n90\t| Test File | Test Description | Reason |\n91\t|-----------|------------------|--------|\n92\t| `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts` | archive contract schemas accept all Epic 7 entry kinds and reject non-finalized entries | Protects shared contract vocabulary before route work |\n93\t| `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts` | live history upserts still update current process history without creating archive rows | Protects live/archive separation |\n94\t| `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` maps `process_message` to `model_message` only for finalized compatible items | Compatibility bridge clarity |\n95\t| `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | same `processId + finalizationKey` returns or no-ops existing archive row | Primitive idempotency guard below Story 2 service proofs |\n96\t| `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | pre-user-message entries form deterministic turn zero | Edge case in grouping rules |\n97\t| `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | turn-cache rebuild preserves stable turn provenance for derived views | Prevents dangling view references after rebuild |\n98\t| `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `chunk_candidate` rejects generated summary body content | Prevents summarization scope creep |\n99\t| `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | stale derived views are rebuilt from current turns without breaking archive reads | Covers rebuild consistency after new archive entries |\n100\t| `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | sequence assignment is atomic across same-process appends | Protects ordering under concurrent writes |\n101\t| `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | derived-view refresh conflict returns `ARCHIVE_DERIVATION_CONFLICT` | Error contract coverage |\n102\t| `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | invalid archive query returns `INVALID_ARCHIVE_REQUEST` | Error contract coverage |\n103\t\n104\t## Chunk Test Counts\n105\t\n106\t| Chunk | TC Tests | Non-TC Tests | Total | Primary Files |\n107\t|-------|----------|--------------|-------|---------------|\n108\t| 0 Foundation | 0 | 1 | 1 | contract/schema/fixture tests |\n109\t| 1 Archive persistence | 9 | 2 | 11 | Convex archive entries |\n110\t| 2 Finalization boundary | 5 | 2 | 7 | archive finalization, live tests |\n111\t| 3 Archive read/reopen | 7 | 1 | 8 | archive API, client archive section |\n112\t| 4 Turn derivation | 5 | 2 | 7 | turn derivation service |\n113\t| 5 Structural views | 7 | 3 | 10 | derived-view service/client |\n114\t| 6 Provenance coherence | 4 | 0 | 4 | archive API enrichment |\n115\t| 7 Reopen/bounded reads | 4 | 0 | 4 | archive API, derived-view service |\n116\t| **Total** | **41** | **11** | **52** |  |\n117\t\n118\tEpic 7 has 41 named TCs. Non-TC tests cover live/archive separation,\n119\tcompatibility mapping, turn-zero grouping, turn-cache rebuild stability,\n120\tno-summary enforcement, stale/rebuilt derived views, primitive idempotency, atomic sequence\n121\tassignment, invalid archive requests, and refresh conflict behavior.\n122\t\n123\t## Verification Gates\n124\t\n125\t| Phase | Command | Expected Result |\n126\t|-------|---------|-----------------|\n127\t| Skeleton / Red exit | `pnpm run red-verify` | Format, lint, typecheck, and build pass while new behavior tests fail against stubs |\n128\t| Development | `pnpm run verify` | Standard project verification passes |\n129\t| Green exit | `pnpm run green-verify` | All tests pass and no-test-change guard runs |\n130\t| Story/Epic completion | `pnpm run verify-all` | Full verification, integration, and e2e scaffold pass |\n131\t\n132\t## Manual Verification Checklist\n133\t\n134\t1. Start Convex with `pnpm run convex:dev`.\n135\t2. Start app server with `pnpm dev`.\n136\t3. Run or simulate a process that finalizes user, model, tool, and process-event entries.\n137\t4. Open the process archive surface and verify finalized entries are visible in order.\n138\t5. Reload the process and verify archive entries remain visible without environment state.\n139\t6. Open the turn view and verify turns reference source archive entries.\n140\t7. Open derived views and verify structural turn ranges/chunk candidates have no generated summary text.\n141\t8. Simulate missing related source/artifact context and verify only affected entries degrade.\n142\t9. Verify archive reads return a bounded page with a next cursor.\n143\t\n144\t## Reconciliation\n145\t\n146\t- TC tests: 41\n147\t- Non-TC decided tests: 11\n148\t- Planned automated tests: 52\n149\t- Manual verification steps: 9\n150\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ceb8cd2b-35ba-478c-a9f5-82f59e9dd21d","uuid":"1054f0e3-345f-4603-aa38-580d1e5463fa","timestamp":"2026-05-05T23:30:35.887Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md","content":"# Test Plan: Epic 7 Archive and Derived Views\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis test plan maps every Epic 7 test condition to planned tests. It verifies\ncanonical archive append/read behavior, finalization boundaries, archive read\nsurfaces, turn derivation, structural derived views, provenance enrichment, and\ndegraded reads.\n\nRelated design: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md`\n\n## Test Strategy\n\n### Test Layers\n\n| Layer | Files | Purpose |\n|-------|-------|---------|\n| Convex service tests | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts`, `convex/archiveTurns.test.ts`, `convex/derivedArchiveViews.test.ts` | Durable append/read, sequence, idempotency, cached projections |\n| Fastify service/API tests | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | Auth/access, finalization policy, archive reads, derivation, degraded states |\n| Clien