ent/daytona-provider-adapter.ts:574:      archiveEntries: (obj.archiveEntries as ExecutionResult['archiveEntries']) ?? [],\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:28:- `ArchiveReadService.getArchive`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:135:| Process/archive UI entry | `apps/platform/client/features/processes/archive-section.ts`, `apps/platform/client/app/bootstrap.ts` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:140:- Archive reads depend on durable `archiveEntries`, not live WebSocket state or environment state.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:141:- `ArchiveReadService` returns a bounded page of canonical archive entries for the route and preserves any per-entry degraded status present on the response contract.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:155:| TC-3.1a | `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts` | archive entries visible |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:156:| TC-3.1b | `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts` | empty archive state visible |\napps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:43:      finalizationKey: buildHistoryItemArchiveFinalizationKey({\napps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:61:export function buildHistoryItemArchiveFinalizationKey(args: {\napps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:67:      return buildAcceptedUserResponseArchiveFinalizationKey(args.sourceObjectId);\napps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:77:export function buildAcceptedUserResponseArchiveFinalizationKey(historyItemId: string): string {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:38:| Current `processHistoryItems` vocabulary differs from canonical archive taxonomy | Baseline, Tech Design Question 2 | Design adds new `archiveEntries` while bridging current history for compatibility. No historical migration/backfill is included. | Resolved - clarified |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:39:| Finalization boundary must prevent raw deltas and interrupted partial objects | AC-2.x, Tech Design Question 3 | Design introduces `ArchiveFinalizationService` and `finalizationKey` idempotency. Only completed objects call append. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:40:| Turn and derived-view persistence could accidentally become canonical truth | AC-4.x, AC-5.x | Design treats turns and derived views as cached/rebuildable projections over `archiveEntries`. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:53:| 1 | What durable schema stores archive entries, sequence numbers, related references, and idempotency keys? | Add `archiveEntries` with `projectId`, `processId`, `entryKind`, `sequence`, `finalizationKey`, `sourceObjectId`, body fields, related ids, status, and timestamps. Convex assigns sequence inside an append mutation and enforces `finalizationKey` idempotency per process. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:55:| 3 | What finalization boundary determines when entries are archived? | `ArchiveFinalizationService` is called only from completion points: accepted user responses, completed model/runtime objects, completed script emissions, finalized tool calls/results, and process events. Raw live deltas and interrupted partial objects never call append. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:57:| 5 | Should turns be persisted, computed on read, or cached with rebuild? | Turns are cached derived records in `archiveTurns` for bounded reads, but they are rebuildable from `archiveEntries` and never canonical truth. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:60:| 8 | What pagination/indexing keeps reads bounded? | Convex indexes `archiveEntries` by `processId, sequence`, `archiveTurns` by `processId, turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:108:    FINAL[ArchiveFinalizationService]\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:111:    READ[ArchiveReadService]\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:112:    DERIVE[TurnDerivationService]\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:113:    VIEWS[DerivedArchiveViewService]\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:129:`ArchiveFinalizationService` when a process object is complete. The service\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:133:The read path is broader. Fastify routes call `ArchiveReadService` for archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:134:entries, `TurnDerivationService` for turns, and `DerivedArchiveViewService` for\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:143:| Add new `archiveEntries` instead of replacing `processHistoryItems` | Current history is presentation-oriented and already used by live process surfaces | Epic 7 can preserve archive truth without destabilizing current UI |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:146:| Turns are cached projections | Long processes need bounded turn reads, but turns are derived | `archiveTurns` can be rebuilt from `archiveEntries` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:157:├── archiveEntries.ts                         # NEW: append/read canonical archive entries\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:158:├── archiveTurns.ts                           # NEW: cached derived turn records\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:159:├── derivedArchiveViews.ts                    # NEW: structural derived-view records\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:177:├── derived-archive-view.service.ts           # NEW: structural view creation/read/refresh\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:189:├── archive-section.ts                        # NEW: process archive read surface\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:190:├── archive-turns-section.ts                  # NEW: derived turn surface\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:191:└── derived-archive-views-section.ts          # NEW: structural derived-view surface\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:201:├── service/client/archive-section.test.ts    # NEW: client archive rendering tests\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:202:├── service/client/archive-turns-section.test.ts # NEW: turn surface rendering tests\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:203:└── service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts # NEW: derived-view UI tests\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:210:| `convex/archiveEntries.ts` | New | Append/read canonical entries, sequence assignment, idempotency guard, pagination | Convex schema | AC-1.x, AC-2.3, AC-3.x, AC-7.3 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:211:| `convex/archiveTurns.ts` | New | Store rebuildable cached turns | Convex schema | AC-4.x, AC-7.1 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:212:| `convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts` | New | Store/read structural derived views | Convex schema | AC-5.x, AC-7.x |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:213:| `ArchiveFinalizationService` | New | Map completed process objects to archive entries; exclude deltas/partials | PlatformStore | AC-1.x, AC-2.x |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:214:| `ArchiveReadService` | New | Read archive entries, enforce access via routes/services, enrich related context, degrade locally | PlatformStore, artifact/source services | AC-3.x, AC-6.x, AC-7.x |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:215:| `TurnDerivationService` | New | Deterministically derive/rebuild turns from archive entries | PlatformStore | AC-4.x |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:216:| `DerivedArchiveViewService` | New | Build/read non-summarizing structural views | PlatformStore, TurnDerivationService | AC-5.x, AC-7.x |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:217:| `ProcessHistoryCompatService` | New | Bridge archive entries to existing history surfaces without migration | ArchiveReadService | A7, Story 0 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:223:### Convex `archiveEntries`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:236:export const archiveEntriesTableFields = {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:273:### Convex `archiveTurns`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:276:export const archiveTurnsTableFields = {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:281:  archiveEntryIds: v.array(v.id('archiveEntries')),\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:298:not canonical. `TurnDerivationService.rebuildTurns` must upsert turns by stable\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:302:### Convex `derivedArchiveViews`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:305:export const derivedArchiveViewsTableFields = {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:312:  sourceArchiveEntryIds: v.array(v.id('archiveEntries')),\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:333:The array fields in `archiveTurns` and `derivedArchiveViews` are intentionally\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:389:export interface DerivedArchiveView {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:408:| Get process archive | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive` | `ArchiveReadService.getArchive` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:409:| Get process turns | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/turns` | `TurnDerivationService.getTurns` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:410:| Get derived archive views | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/derived-views` | `DerivedArchiveViewService.listViews` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:411:| Refresh derived archive views | POST | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/derived-views/refresh` | `DerivedArchiveViewService.refreshViews` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:447:export interface ArchiveFinalizationService {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:469:export interface ArchiveReadService {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:479:export interface TurnDerivationService {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:492:export interface DerivedArchiveViewService {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:497:  }): Promise<{ views: DerivedArchiveView[] }>;\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:503:  }): Promise<{ views: DerivedArchiveView[]; refreshStatus: 'settled' | 'accepted' | 'degraded' }>;\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:545:  replaceDerivedArchiveViews(args: {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:548:    views: DerivedArchiveView[];\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:551:  listDerivedArchiveViews(args: {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:553:  }): Promise<DerivedArchiveView[]>;\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:575:    participant X as Convex archiveEntries\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:590:objects that reach a finalization point call `ArchiveFinalizationService`,\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:606:environment state or live WebSocket state. `ArchiveReadService` fetches one\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:613:canonical `archiveEntries` row unless the row itself was originally persisted\napps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:14:export interface ArchiveReadService {\napps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:24:export class DefaultArchiveReadService implements ArchiveReadService {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/002-epic-verifier-batch.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"2f84684a-a0cf-4ae8-bc51-e485762f54fb\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The archive primitive, turn derivation, and derived-view layers are implemented against the full Epic 7 taxonomy, but the live execution/finalization path still feeds them legacy `ProcessHistoryItem` data, so later stories are validated against seeded archive rows instead of the real runtime source.\",\"Story 6 provenance enrichment is disconnected from Stories 2-3 production writes: archive reads can enrich `relatedArtifactVersionId` and `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, but the shipped append paths never persist those IDs.\",\"The archive page, turn page, and derived-view page all work when archive rows already exist, but the default shipped execution flow does not generate the archive shape those stories were designed around.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"`ExecutionResult` is still typed as `processHistoryItems: ProcessHistoryItem[]`, and `ProcessHistoryItem` still exposes the legacy presentation vocabulary rather than the canonical archive taxonomy.\",\"The design contract said archive rows would store nullable artifact/source/tool IDs and read services would enrich later; current checkpoint/provenance interfaces do not return the identifiers needed to realize that contract on the live path.\",\"The process work-surface contract/UI never added the designed archive entry point, so archive/turn/view routes are not connected to the primary process surface.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"`corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` both exited 0.\",\"Automation is masking the main integration gaps: tests such as `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` and `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` seed canonical archive rows directly, and `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` seeds provenance-linked rows directly, instead of proving the live runtime can emit them.\",\"The gate is still lighter than the epic implies: `guard:no-test-changes` prints `SKIP` and `test:e2e` is scaffold-only, so there is no executable end-to-end check for live archive generation or archive navigation.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"`createApp` wires `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` by default, and that service still uses the documented Epic 3 default placeholder payload; the placeholder emits a synthetic `process_event` plus \\\"Execution placeholder...\\\" side-work output rather than real low-level archive material.\",\"No production archive append path populates `relatedArtifactVersionId`, `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, or `relatedToolCallId`; the live appenders explicitly write those fields as `null`, so provenance and tool-correlation behavior is unreachable from real traffic.\",\"Checkpoint persistence and source-provenance recording happen only after archive finalization and expose no archive-linkable identifiers back to the archive writer, so Story 6 enrichment currently works only for pre-seeded/test-fixture rows.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-E7-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Live execution cannot emit the Epic 7 archive taxonomy\",\"evidence\":\"`ProcessHistoryItem` only allows `user_message|process_message|progress_update|attention_request|side_work_update|process_event` in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:124-131`, and `ExecutionResult` still exposes `processHistoryItems: ProcessHistoryItem[]` in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts:125-132`. `ProcessHistoryCompatService` only maps `user_message`, `process_message`, and `process_event` into archive kinds in `apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:8-23`. On the shipped path, `createApp` defaults to `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` in `apps/platform/server/app.ts:285-286`, and that default service still uses the documented Epic 3 placeholder payload in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:159-177`, which emits only a synthetic `process_event` in `script-execution.service.ts:85-128`. As a result, the runtime cannot produce `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result` archive entries at all, and does not produce real `model_message` traffic without a non-default injected runner.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-1.2\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-E7-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Archive rows never capture artifact/source provenance on the live path\",\"evidence\":\"Both live archive appenders hardcode relation fields to `null`: `apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:39-56` and `apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:151-167`. During execution, archive finalization happens before provenance recording in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:563-581` and `690-706`; later checkpoint/provenance steps run separately in `process-environment.service.ts:829-882`. Those downstream interfaces do not return linkable identifiers: `persistCheckpointArtifacts` returns only `PlatformProcessOutputSummary[]` in `apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:386-389`, and `SourceProvenanceService.recordInformedWorkForCurrentSources` / `recordReceivedCodeUpdates` both return `Promise<void>` in `apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:22-34`. The read-time enrichment added for Story 6 therefore depends on IDs that production never writes.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\",\"AC-6.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-E7-003\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Process work surface never exposes an archive entry point\",\"evidence\":\"`renderProcessWorkSurfacePage` accepts callbacks for project, review, start, resume, rehydrate, rebuild, and respond only in `apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts:27-45`, and its control switch has no archive navigation case in `process-work-surface-page.ts:140-169`. The shared control contract likewise only defines `start`, `respond`, `resume`, `rehydrate`, `rebuild`, `review`, and `restart` in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:176-206`. The archive route exists, but it is not discoverable from the primary process surface.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"BROWSER-ROUTE-CONTRACT\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"`verify-all` passed, but `test:e2e` is scaffold-only and `guard:no-test-changes` is not implemented, so those gate layers remain unproven.\",\"This review did not manually run `pnpm run convex:dev` and `pnpm dev` to validate archive generation against a live backend/provider session.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"b4ca1d64-d1f4-434e-a365-46beb9748d92\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The route, store, client, and test surfaces for archive/turn/view reads are wired end to end, and both `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` passed.\",\"Cross-story drift remains between the Story 1/2 write path and the Story 4/5/6 read path: turns, derived views, and provenance enrichment assume a richer canonical archive than the shipped execution path actually produces.\",\"Most low-level archive taxonomy and provenance scenarios are proven with fixtures/in-memory stores rather than by the real execution pipeline.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The tech design says Fastify should finalize completed model/runtime objects, script emissions, and tool call/result pairs into canonical archive entries, but the implementation still canonicalizes runtime output through presentation-level `processHistoryItems` compatibility mapping.\",\"The design says `archiveTurns` are cached projections for bounded reads, but turn and derived-view GETs rebuild from full archive scans on each request instead of serving cached projections first.\",\"The design expects archive entries to carry nullable artifact/source/tool foreign keys for read-time enrichment, but the shipped writers persist provenance on parallel tables without linking those ids back onto archive rows.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Story 3-5 read surfaces are present and exercised by tests, including access control, empty states, degraded rendering, and derived-view conflict handling.\",\"Story 1-2 are only partially realized on the production path: canonical append currently reaches `user_message`, `model_message`, and `process_event`, not the full seven-kind archive taxonomy required by the epic.\",\"Story 6 provenance coherence is implemented as a read-time enrichment layer, but the write path never supplies the archive-side ids that would let real archive entries surface artifact/source provenance.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The default execution path still runs the explicit placeholder script payload in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts`, and that payload emits a single finalized `process_event` instead of real low-level reasoning/script/tool archive objects.\",\"Artifact checkpoints and source-provenance records are persisted on side channels, but the shipped archive writers never attach `relatedArtifactVersionId` or `relatedSourceProvenanceId` to canonical archive entries.\",\"Archive source-provenance enrichment only looks at the newest 200 provenance rows for a process, so older archive pages can report healthy links as degraded once real archive rows start linking to older provenance ids.\",\"Turn and derived-view reads currently pay full-archive rebuild cost on every request rather than using cached projections as the primary bounded read path.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-07-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"The shipped archive write path never produces four of the seven required canonical entry kinds\",\"evidence\":\"`ExecutionResult` only carries `processHistoryItems`, outputs, side-work writes, and checkpoint candidates (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts:125-132`). `processHistoryItemKindSchema` is limited to `user_message`, `process_message`, `progress_update`, `attention_request`, `side_work_update`, and `process_event` (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:124-131`). Runtime execution stores those history items and then archives them through `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`), while `ProcessHistoryCompatService` only maps `user_message`, `process_message`, and `process_event` into archive entries and hard-codes the related ids to `null` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:8-12`, `:39-56`). The default production script payload is still the shared placeholder and only emits a finalized `process_event` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:15-135`, `:158-163`). As shipped, the real path never emits `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result` archive entries.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-1.2\",\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-07-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Archive provenance coherence is unreachable on the real write path because archive rows never record related artifact/source ids\",\"evidence\":\"Accepted user-response archiving explicitly writes `relatedArtifactVersionId: null` and `relatedSourceProvenanceId: null` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:151-167`). The compatibility archive path also hard-codes all related ids to `null` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:39-56`). Meanwhile the execution/checkpoint flow persists artifacts and source provenance on separate paths via `persistCheckpointArtifacts`, `recordInformedWorkForCurrentSources`, and `recordReceivedCodeUpdates` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:577-581`, `:830-883`), and `SourceProvenanceService` creates durable provenance rows separately (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:200-218`). Because no shipped archive writer threads those ids back onto archive entries, the Story 6 enrichment surface is only reachable from fixtures/tests, not from real archive data.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-07-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Source provenance enrichment can falsely degrade older archive entries because it only loads the newest 200 provenance rows\",\"evidence\":\"`listProcessSourceProvenanceEntries` returns only the 200 most recent source-provenance records for a process (`convex/sourceProvenance.ts:58-71`). `ArchiveReadService` loads that process-wide slice once when any page contains `relatedSourceProvenanceId` values (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:120-126`) and resolves each entry from that in-memory map (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:148-160`). If an archive page references an older but still-existing provenance id outside the newest 200 rows, the entry is incorrectly degraded with `Related source provenance is unavailable.` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:198-200`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"convex/sourceProvenance.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.4\",\"AC-6.2\",\"AC-6.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EV-07-004\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Turn and derived-view reads bypass the cached-projection design and rescan the full archive on every request\",\"evidence\":\"`getTurns` always calls `rebuildTurns` before reading a page (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:61-85`), and `rebuildTurns` paginates through the entire archive (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:89-110`). `listViews` and `refreshViews` likewise rebuild turns and recompute full-archive signatures by scanning all archive entries before responding (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:50-86`, `:100-143`, `:148-182`). Functionally this works, but it drifts from the tech design's cached/bounded projection model for long-running processes.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"The 2-second performance NFR for turn/archive reads at 5,000 archive entries was not measured against a real Convex-backed runtime during this review.\",\"Manual end-to-end verification with `pnpm run convex:dev` and `pnpm dev` was not performed; production-path conclusions are based on code inspection plus automated test results.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/002-epic-verifier-batch.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T09:15:32.432Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T09:25:20.895Z\"}\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:23:import { ArchiveFinalizationService } from '../../archive/archive-finalization.service.js';\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:71:      ArchiveFinalizationService,\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:73:    > = new ArchiveFinalizationService(platformStore),\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:598:        archiveEntries: sideEffects.deferredArchiveEntries,\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:736:    for (const archiveEntry of args.executionResult.archiveEntries ?? []) {\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:783:    archiveEntries: RuntimeArchiveEntry[];\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:795:    for (const archiveEntry of args.archiveEntries) {\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:1019:          archiveEntries: args.deferredArchiveEntries,\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:1103:        archiveEntries: args.deferredArchiveEntries,\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/003-epic-verifier-batch.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"67138ffb-df0f-4ac8-8ea2-ae7ae3d35994\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 1-7 are wired end-to-end through shared contracts, Convex tables, Fastify routes, and client archive surfaces, and both requested verification gates succeeded.\",\"The cross-story happy path works, but the execution-to-archive handoff still breaks canonical-truth guarantees in two places: production runs emit placeholder archive content, and deferred entries are dropped instead of downgraded when provenance/checkpoint resolution fails.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The archive storage/read architecture is coherent, but the execution boundary drifts from the tech design: `createApp` composes a real provider registry while `ScriptExecutionService` still defaults to a canned payload instead of a process-specific runtime.\",\"Turn and derived-view GET reads rebuild projections on every request rather than primarily serving cached projections, which weakens the bounded-read strategy described in the tech design for long histories.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Implemented coverage is strong on the green path: archive persistence, archive APIs, turn derivation, derived-view responses, and provenance enrichment all shipped and `corepack pnpm run green-verify` plus `corepack pnpm run verify-all` both succeeded.\",\"Coverage is incomplete on degraded production behavior: there is no protection against losing deferred canonical entries when artifact/source linkage cannot be resolved at append time.\",\"The epic gate passed, but the `test:e2e` leg is still scaffold-only, so no executable browser/runtime end-to-end archive scenario is currently enforced by automation.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The in-memory/failing provider adapters and stub checkpoint writer are clearly test-only seams and are not the material concern.\",\"The material non-real production path is `ScriptExecutionService`'s default payload, which fabricates a `Default Execution Summary`, canned reasoning/tool/model/process archive entries, and a dummy source checkpoint note for writable repos.\",\"When deferred archive entries depend on artifact or source provenance, the production orchestrator currently skips the entry entirely if that relation cannot be resolved, creating a missing-history path instead of a degraded-but-readable canonical archive record.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Production executions still archive placeholder output instead of real process work\",\"evidence\":\"The production composition root instantiates `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` with no custom payload factory (`apps/platform/server/app.ts:285-286`), so runtime execution falls back to `buildDefaultScriptPayload`. That default script writes a `Default Execution Summary`, emits canned `reasoning`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, `model_message`, `process_event`, and `script_emission` archive entries, and stages a dummy writable-source file with commit message `Record default execution note` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:15-317`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Deferred archive entries are silently dropped when provenance or checkpoint relations cannot be resolved\",\"evidence\":\"The orchestrator defers entries with `artifactCheckpointIndex` or `sourceProvenanceBinding`, but `appendDeferredArchiveEntries` uses `continue` when the related artifact version or source provenance record is missing (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:783-810`). A direct repro against that helper returned `{\\\"entries\\\":[],\\\"page\\\":{\\\"cursor\\\":null,\\\"nextCursor\\\":null,\\\"hasMore\\\":false}}` after attempting to append a deferred `script_emission` entry with unresolved relations, so canonical history is lost instead of surfaced as degraded metadata.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.3\",\"AC-7.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Turn and derived-view reads bypass the intended cache-first bounded-read design\",\"evidence\":\"Every `GET /archive/turns` request forces `rebuildTurns` before listing turns (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:61-85`), and `GET /archive/derived-views` likewise rebuilds turns and rewrites stored views on read (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:50-75`). This preserves correctness today but adds avoidable full-archive work and write amplification on normal reads.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-7.1\",\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Decide whether the placeholder execution payload is an explicit temporary stopgap or an unintended leftover from Epic 3; either way it should not ship as canonical archive truth.\",\"No executable e2e suite currently verifies the browser/runtime archive flow because `test:e2e` is scaffold-only.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"7e8e159e-b398-4820-ad73-1e4ceb24971c\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Canonical archive append/read, turn derivation, derived-view routes, and client surfaces are implemented end to end, and both `green-verify` and `verify-all` passed.\",\"The degraded-state story is inconsistent across surfaces: archive-entry degradation is computed in the archive read service, but turn and derived-view rebuilds read raw archive rows and can report the same process slice as `ready`.\",\"The deferred finalization path is not lossless. Under partial artifact/provenance failure it can drop finalized entries entirely, which breaks reopen consistency and any later turn/view derivation that depends on the archive as canonical truth.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"`ArchiveReadService` bypasses the existing source-provenance read service and rehydrates source provenance from raw store rows, so archive-source coherence can drift from the rest of the source domain.\",\"Flow 7 in the tech design says archive, turns, and derived views use cursor-bounded reads; derived views currently implement only a hard `slice(0, 50)` with no cursor/query contract.\",\"The production runtime still exercises archive finalization through the shared default placeholder script payload rather than process-type-specific execution logic.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Happy-path coverage is strong: durable archive tables, archive routes, turn rebuilds, structural derived views, provenance enrichment, and client rendering are all present and exercised by passing tests.\",\"Coverage is weak for degraded reopen scenarios. The existing suites assert missing-record degradation on archive reads, but they do not catch deferred-entry loss, turn/view degradation drift, or source-detach/access-revocation behavior after reopen.\",\"Epic 7 is close on the happy path, but the current implementation does not fully preserve the 'archive stays visible and projections degrade locally' contract under partial-failure conditions.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"I did not find the in-memory provider fake wired into production; the material non-real path is the real runtime default in `ScriptExecutionService`, which still emits a canned 'default execution payload'.\",\"`appendDeferredArchiveEntries` has a lossy production branch: unresolved artifact/source bindings cause the code to skip the finalized entry instead of persisting a degraded canonical row.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Deferred archive entries are silently dropped when related artifact or source provenance cannot be resolved\",\"evidence\":\"`appendDeferredArchiveEntries` resolves `artifactCheckpointIndex` / `sourceProvenanceBinding` and then `continue`s when either lookup is missing (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts` lines 783-810). That drops finalized deferred entries instead of appending a degraded archive row, violating the archive-truth requirement when checkpoint/provenance side effects partially fail.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.3\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Turn and derived-view rebuilds ignore related-context degradation computed by archive reads\",\"evidence\":\"`TurnDerivationService.rebuildTurns` pages raw archive rows from `platformStore.listArchiveEntries` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts` lines 48-50 and 89-111) and only degrades turns when the stored row already has `entryStatus === 'degraded'` (lines 149-154). Missing artifact/source context is added later by `ArchiveReadService` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts` lines 163-224), so turns and derived views can stay `ready` while the archive page shows degraded entries.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.4\",\"AC-5.5\",\"AC-7.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Archive reopen bypasses source-provenance degradation logic for detached or revoked sources\",\"evidence\":\"`ArchiveReadService` loads raw `StoredSourceProvenanceRecord` rows and copies their stored `entryStatus` / `degradationReason` directly into archive responses (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts` lines 120-125 and 198-212). The actual read-time degradation logic for detached/redacted/unavailable sources lives in `DefaultSourceProvenanceService.listProcessSourceProvenance` / `buildSourceProvenanceEntry` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts` lines 153-199 and 223-285). A source that later detaches or loses access will still read as `ready` in the archive.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.2\",\"AC-6.3\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-004\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Derived-view reads are bounded but not cursor-paginated as designed\",\"evidence\":\"Flow 7 says archive entries, turns, and derived views use cursor pagination with default limits (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md` lines 668-674). The derived-view route schema has no querystring contract (`apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts` lines 37-46), and the service simply `slice(0, 50)`s the computed set (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts` lines 210-211).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EV-005\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production execution still runs through a placeholder default script payload\",\"evidence\":\"`ScriptExecutionService` builds a canned 'default execution payload' with fixed artifact/tool/archive output text (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts` lines 15-18 and 52-60), placeholder side-work summaries (`lines 233-236`), and an explicit comment that process-type-specific payloads 'come later' (`lines 279-283`). This is a real runtime default, not just test infrastructure.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"`green-verify` and `verify-all` both passed, but `guard:no-test-changes` currently prints `SKIP`, so the story gate's extra protection is scaffolded rather than enforced.\",\"Whether the placeholder default execution payload is accepted temporary debt outside Epic 7 needs an explicit product/architecture ruling before treating the archive path as production-real.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/003-epic-verifier-batch.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T09:51:17.378Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T09:59:52.997Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/06-archive-provenance-coherence/004-implementor.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-implement\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"20b4267f-e234-481f-a4ca-f8207b3ac24a\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"role\":\"story_implementor\",\"sessionId\":\"019df6fa-a664-73a3-ac32-65ff8278cbfe\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df6fa-a664-73a3-ac32-65ff8278cbfe\",\"storyId\":\"06-archive-provenance-coherence\"},\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"06-archive-provenance-coherence\",\"title\":\"Story 6: Archive Provenance Coherence\"},\"planSummary\":\"Extended archive reads with read-time artifact/source provenance enrichment, preserved canonical rows by layering enrichment only in the archive read service, surfaced the new provenance in the archive UI, and added Story 6 API/client coverage for happy-path and degraded lookup behavior.\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts\",\"reason\":\"Extended the archive entry contract with optional artifact-version and source-provenance enrichment payloads.\"},{\"path\":\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\",\"reason\":\"Added read-time provenance enrichment, producing-process lookup, and per-entry degradation when related artifact/source context cannot be resolved.\"},{\"path\":\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/archive-section.ts\",\"reason\":\"Rendered related artifact-version, producing-process, and source provenance details on archive entries when present.\"},{\"path\":\"tests/fixtures/archive.ts\",\"reason\":\"Added enriched archive-entry fixtures for artifact and source provenance scenarios.\"},{\"path\":\"tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Added Story 6 server coverage for artifact/source provenance visibility and per-entry degradation while seeding the in-memory store with related provenance data.\"},{\"path\":\"tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Added client coverage proving enriched archive provenance renders in the archive section.\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[],\"modified\":[\"tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts\"],\"removed\":[]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm exec biome check --formatter-enabled=true --linter-enabled=true --assist-enabled=false apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts apps/platform/client/features/processes/archive-section.ts tests/fixtures/archive.ts tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts && corepack pnpm vitest tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"selfReview\":{\"passesRun\":0,\"findingsFixed\":[\"Archive reads now enrich related artifact versions with producing-process provenance without mutating canonical archive storage.\",\"Archive entries now degrade only the affected row when related source or artifact provenance cannot be resolved at read time.\",\"Archive UI and tests now prove enriched provenance remains visible on the existing Story 3 surface.\"],\"findingsSurfaced\":[]},\"openQuestions\":[],\"specDeviations\":[],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Proceed to story verification focused on Story 6 acceptance criteria and archive provenance regression review.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/06-archive-provenance-coherence/004-implementor.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T07:11:54.758Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T07:21:44.214Z\"}\napps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:10:import { ArchiveFinalizationService } from '../archive/archive-finalization.service.js';\napps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:11:import { buildAcceptedUserResponseArchiveFinalizationKey } from '../archive/process-history-compat.service.js';\napps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:24:      ArchiveFinalizationService,\napps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:26:    > = new ArchiveFinalizationService(platformStore),\napps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:155:      finalizationKey: buildAcceptedUserResponseArchiveFinalizationKey(\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:253:  archiveEntries: [],\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/004-implementor.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-implement\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"7f0819cf-105c-474a-b781-2ea7640bc871\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"role\":\"story_implementor\",\"sessionId\":\"019df60d-fe28-78c2-89a0-54aa6e77481e\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df60d-fe28-78c2-89a0-54aa6e77481e\",\"storyId\":\"01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence\"},\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence\",\"title\":\"Story 1: Canonical Archive Entry Persistence\"},\"planSummary\":\"Implemented the Story 1 Convex archive append/read primitive, including per-process sequence assignment, process-scoped finalization-key idempotency, stable ascending reads by sequence, related-context id round-tripping, and persistence-focused coverage for the canonical archive entry contract.\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"convex/archiveEntries.ts\",\"reason\":\"Added the real Convex mutation/query implementation for canonical archive entry append/read with validation, process ownership checks, idempotent replay handling, sequence assignment, and bounded page responses.\"},{\"path\":\"convex/archiveEntries.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Added Story 1 persistence tests covering accepted kinds, unsupported kind rejection, stable ordering, same-timestamp determinism, replay idempotency, related-context ids, and per-process sequence behavior.\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[\"convex/archiveEntries.test.ts\"],\"modified\":[],\"removed\":[],\"totalAfterStory\":663,\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\":7},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm exec vitest run convex/archiveEntries.test.ts --environment node\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"selfReview\":{\"passesRun\":0,\"findingsFixed\":[\"Implemented the missing Convex archive persistence surface instead of leaving Story 1 at schema-only foundation state.\",\"Aligned stored archive-entry invariants with the shared contract by validating non-empty finalization keys and optional ids, structured-body requirements, and degraded-entry reasons.\",\"Verified the final tree with both story and epic gates after the last validation pass.\"],\"findingsSurfaced\":[\"Biome still reports a pre-existing non-blocking style info in packages/lbuild-impl/tests/unit/sdk/story-orchestrate-status.test.ts:173 that is outside this story’s scope.\"]},\"openQuestions\":[],\"specDeviations\":[],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Proceed to Story 2 and wire finalized live/process completion points into this appendArchiveEntry primitive through the archive finalization service.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/004-implementor.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T02:53:25.185Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T03:04:05.956Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/006-epic-synthesis.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-synthesize\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"needs-fixes\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"410b4666-dc99-4b5e-9093-dc18f51088fd\",\"outcome\":\"needs-fixes\",\"confirmedIssues\":[\"The shipped default execution lane still uses the integrated workspace payload from `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts`, which emits `archiveEntries: []` and only a synthetic finalized `process_event`; because `apps/platform/server/app.ts` wires that service by default and `apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts` only bridges legacy history kinds, real production runs still do not generate low-level `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result` archive entries without a custom injected runner.\",\"Archive read-time provenance enrichment can still falsely degrade older archive rows: `apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-entry-enrichment.ts` resolves source provenance from `listProcessSourceProvenance`, but `convex/sourceProvenance.ts` only loads the newest 200 provenance records for a process, so archive entries linked to older provenance IDs can be treated as missing context even when the provenance row still exists.\"],\"disputedOrUnconfirmedIssues\":[\"Earlier verifier findings about deferred archive appends, stale turn/view caches, and missing derived-view pagination are not supported by the current code: deferred entries are appended immediately and later patched, archive append/patch invalidates cached turns/views, derived-view responses are cursor-paginated, and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` now passes.\",\"The process work-surface still does not expose an obvious archive navigation control, but the epic artifacts reviewed here do not make that a clear closeout blocker.\"],\"readinessAssessment\":\"Epic 7 is not ready for closeout yet. The epic gate now passes (`corepack pnpm run verify-all`), but the current implementation still has a real production-path archive gap in the default execution lane and a remaining provenance-enrichment correctness bug for long histories. Separately, `corepack pnpm run green-verify` is not green in the current workspace because `guard:no-test-changes` fails against `HEAD`.\",\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Replace or override the default integrated runtime payload with a process-specific execution producer that emits real canonical archive entries on the live path, fix source-provenance enrichment so archive-linked provenance can be resolved beyond the latest 200 rows, then rerun `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all`.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/006-epic-synthesis.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T13:05:47.001Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T13:12:00.005Z\"}\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts:156:  archiveEntries?: RuntimeArchiveEntry[];\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts:242:      archiveEntries: [],\napps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts:336:      archiveEntries: [],\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/005-epic-verifier-batch.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"c143b247-c13b-48cd-ac42-7cf34522e355\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The derived-view pagination change is only partially propagated: shared contracts, route/schema wiring, the derived-view service, PlatformStore implementations, and several test doubles no longer agree on the `listDerivedArchiveViews` request/response shape.\",\"Turn and derived-view cache behavior now diverges between the in-memory test store and the Convex production store, so cross-story reopen behavior is not being validated against the real persistence path.\",\"Archive capture, turn derivation, and derived-view surfaces are conceptually aligned around archive truth, but the default execution path that feeds the archive is still a canned runtime-audit script rather than real process-specific execution.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The tech design says turn and derived-view rebuilds happen on read from canonical archive data; the current services only rebuild when the cached first page is empty, which is weaker than the documented contract.\",\"The architecture expects Fastify pagination contracts to match store and durable-layer contracts end to end; the current derived-view rollout breaks that consistency and fails the type gate before tests can run.\",\"Canonical archive truth is supposed to preserve finalized process work, but the default production executor still synthesizes archive entries from a hard-coded audit payload.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"`corepack pnpm run verify-all` fails in `typecheck`, so none of the Epic 7 service, client, integration, or e2e tests actually execute to green.\",\"The added Story 6/7 tests around detached-source degradation and bounded derived-view pages improve intended coverage, but they currently provide no passing evidence because the build is broken first.\",\"Static inspection found a production-only stale-cache path that the in-memory tests mask, so even a later green test run should explicitly verify Convex-backed reopen/read behavior.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The production app wires `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` by default, and that service's default payload factory emits a synthetic integrated runtime-audit script that fabricates `reasoning`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, `model_message`, `process_event`, and `script_emission` archive entries.\",\"`InMemoryPlatformStore` deletes cached turns and derived views on archive append/patch, but `ConvexPlatformStore` does not, so production can serve stale derived data even though the primary test store self-heals.\",\"No equivalent fake adapter was found in the archive read routes themselves; the material non-real execution paths are the canned script executor and the test-only cache invalidation behavior.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EPIC7-DERIVED-VIEW-PAGINATION-ROLLUP\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Derived-view pagination refactor is incomplete and breaks the epic gate\",\"evidence\":\"Running `corepack pnpm run verify-all` fails in `typecheck` before any Epic 7 tests run. The current rollout leaves `DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService` and multiple store/test implementations disagreeing about the `listDerivedArchiveViews` shape: TypeScript reports `'cursor' does not exist in type '{ processId: string; }'`, `'views' does not exist on type 'DerivedArchiveView[]'`, plus contract failures in `tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts`, and `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts\",\"tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.1\",\"AC-7.1\",\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EPIC7-STale-DERIVED-CACHE-PRODUCTION\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Convex production reads can return stale turns and derived views after new archive entries arrive\",\"evidence\":\"`DefaultTurnDerivationService.getTurns` rebuilds only when the first cached page is empty, and `DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService.listViews` now does the same. In production, `ConvexPlatformStore.appendArchiveEntry` and `patchArchiveEntry` only write archive rows; they never clear `archiveTurns` or `derivedArchiveViews`. By contrast, `InMemoryPlatformStore` explicitly deletes those caches on append/patch and after turn upserts. After the first successful rebuild, later archive appends in Convex can leave `/archive/turns` and `/archive/derived-views` stale indefinitely until an explicit refresh.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-5.1\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EPIC7-SYNTHETIC-ARCHIVE-PRODUCTION-PATH\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"The default production archive capture path still archives a canned runtime-audit script, not real process execution\",\"evidence\":\"`apps/platform/server/app.ts` constructs `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` when no override is injected. The default `ScriptExecutionService` payload factory always returns `buildIntegratedRuntimeAuditPayload`, whose hard-coded TypeScript module writes a runtime report and emits synthetic archive entries for `reasoning`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, `model_message`, `process_event`, and `script_emission`. That means the live production path feeding Epic 7 is still a placeholder execution program rather than real process-specific work.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Rerun `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` after finishing the derived-view pagination rollout; the current review could not observe any post-typecheck test results.\",\"Decide whether the integrated runtime-audit payload is an accepted temporary production path or a release blocker for Epic 7 shipping.\",\"After fixing the cache policy, verify turn and derived-view reopen behavior against the real Convex store, not only `InMemoryPlatformStore`.\"],\"gateResult\":\"fail\"},{\"resultId\":\"fc533748-7b73-42a8-9606-55f12e2f4677\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Archive entry reads and turn derivation are mostly intact, but the derived-view slice is currently broken: `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` passed 15/15 and `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` passed 8/8, while `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` now fails 6 of 7 cases with 500s.\",\"The archive/turn/view layers no longer react consistently to provenance-only degradation. `/archive` re-enriches entries per read, but cached turns/views can stay stale after source detachment or related-context loss.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"A partial derived-view pagination refactor drifted across layers. `DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService` expects paged stored-view reads, but lower store/Convex seams and several callers still assume the older array-returning contract.\",\"Derived projections are only invalidated on archive writes. Source/artifact state changes do not invalidate or recompute `archiveTurns` / derived views, so the rebuildable-projection contract no longer matches the archive read path's degraded-state behavior.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Archive append/read, access checks, and turn derivation still have meaningful coverage: `archive-api.test.ts` passed 15/15 and `turn-derivation.test.ts` passed 8/8 when run directly.\",\"Derived-view coverage is red. `derived-archive-view.test.ts` fails TC-5.1a, TC-5.2a/5.3a/5.3b, the degraded-on-reopen scenario, TC-7.1b, bounded paging, and the derived-view cache invalidation scenario.\",\"Epic 7 is not green end-to-end because Story 5/7 behavior is down and the turn/view degraded-state contract is inconsistent with Story 6 provenance degradation.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The live derived-view read path is materially broken right now. `corepack pnpm vitest run tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` returns 500s for the GET `/archive/derived-views` scenarios, so the structural-view surface is not usable.\",\"Turn and derived-view caches are not refreshed when only related provenance changes. A source detachment can change `/archive` output immediately while `/archive/turns` and cached derived views keep serving pre-detachment readiness.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-07-01\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Derived-view read path is broken by a partially applied pagination contract change\",\"evidence\":\"`corepack pnpm run typecheck` reports `apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts(254,48)` because `listAllStoredViews` is still calling `platformStore.listDerivedArchiveViews({ processId })` while the new signature requires paging, and `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts(417,61)` / `tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts(341,5)` show callers still returning arrays instead of `{ views, page }`. Running `corepack pnpm vitest run tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` now yields 6 failing 500s, and `corepack pnpm vitest run convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` still fails the derived-view primitive expectations.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts\",\"tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts\",\"convex/archiveEntries.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.1\",\"AC-5.2\",\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.5\",\"AC-7.1\",\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-07-02\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Cached turns and derived views do not re-derive when provenance degrades after the archive is written\",\"evidence\":\"`DefaultArchiveReadService` re-enriches archive entries on every read (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:52-65` plus `apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-entry-enrichment.ts:10-152`), but `DefaultTurnDerivationService.getTurns` only rebuilds when the cached turn page is empty (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:87-98`). I reproduced this by building turns, detaching the linked source attachment, and calling `getTurns` again; the second response still returned the original `ready` turn. The derived-view service follows the same cache-first pattern, so reopen behavior can diverge between `/archive`, `/archive/turns`, and cached derived views after source detachment or provenance degradation.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-entry-enrichment.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.4\",\"AC-6.3\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Both named gates are failed, but neither completed a clean full sweep: `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` stopped immediately in `format:check` on `convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts`, so the remaining lint/build/integration stages were not reached in a passing run.\",\"The provenance-staleness regression was reproduced manually at the service layer; there is no current automated regression test covering cache refresh after source detachment.\"],\"gateResult\":\"fail\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/005-epic-verifier-batch.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T11:29:07.087Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T11:48:15.053Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/017-story-orchestrate-resume.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-orchestrate resume\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"blocked\",\"result\":{\"case\":\"completed\",\"outcome\":\"blocked\",\"storyId\":\"01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence\",\"storyRunId\":\"01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence-story-run-001\",\"currentSnapshotPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/story-lead/001-current.json\",\"eventHistoryPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/story-lead/001-events.jsonl\",\"finalPackagePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/story-lead/001-final-package.json\",\"finalPackage\":{\"outcome\":\"blocked\",\"storyRunId\":\"01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence-story-run-001\",\"storyId\":\"01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence\",\"attempt\":1,\"summary\":{\"storyTitle\":\"Story 1: Canonical Archive Entry Persistence\",\"implementedScope\":\"Restored the missing Story 1 Convex archive-entry primitive exports in `convex/archiveEntries.ts`, keeping the work inside the primitive-only scope from ruling 012: validated the required archive taxonomy, enforced process-scoped `finalizationKey` idempotency, assigned per-process sequences inside the append mutation, returned stable sequence-ordered bounded pages, preserved `lifecycleState: finalized`, and round-tripped nullable related ids without expanding into Story 2/3/6 service or enrichment work.\",\"acceptanceRationale\":\"Story-lead could not accept the story because 3 acceptance check(s) remain incomplete.\"},\"evidence\":{\"implementorArtifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"implementor-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/004-implementor.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"implementor-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/015-continue.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"}],\"selfReviewArtifacts\":[],\"verifierArtifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"verifier-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/008-verify.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"verifier-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/014-verify.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"verifier-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/018-verify.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"}],\"quickFixArtifacts\":[],\"callerInputArtifacts\":[],\"gateRuns\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"not-run\"}]},\"verification\":{\"finalVerifierOutcome\":\"pass\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"S1-F1\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":[\"014-verify.json resolved S1-F1 after impl-lead ruling 012 aligned Story 1 to primitive-only evidence.\",\"018-verify.json keeps all primitive-only requirements verified with no open findings.\"]},{\"id\":\"S1-F2\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":[\"014-verify.json resolved S1-F2 as superseded by the current implementation state.\",\"018-verify.json reports no production path findings.\"]},{\"id\":\"S1-F3\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":[\"018-verify.json reports S1-F3 resolved because appendArchiveEntry and listArchiveEntries exports were restored in convex/archiveEntries.ts.\",\"018-verify.json reports both the focused archiveEntries test and green-verify passed.\"]}]},\"riskAndDeviationReview\":{\"specDeviations\":[],\"assumedRisks\":[],\"scopeChanges\":[],\"productionPathDecisionItems\":[]},\"diffReview\":{\"changedFiles\":[],\"storyScopedAssessment\":\"Story-lead package is scoped to orchestration evidence and impl-lead handoff data.\"},\"acceptanceChecks\":[{\"name\":\"story-gate-result\",\"status\":\"unknown\",\"evidence\":[\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\"],\"reasoning\":\"Story gate corepack pnpm run verify-all reported not-run.\"},{\"name\":\"final-verifier-result\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/008-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/014-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/018-verify.json\"],\"reasoning\":