ries visible |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:156:| TC-3.1b | `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts` | empty archive state visible |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:160:| TC-3.3b | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | missing process archive read returns not found |\\n./apps/platform/client/features/processes/archive-section.ts:54:  section.setAttribute('data-archive-section', 'true');\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:6:process archive, turn derivation, and non-summarizing structural derived views.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:19:- Epic: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md`\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:20:- Test plan: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md`\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:38:| Current `processHistoryItems` vocabulary differs from canonical archive taxonomy | Baseline, Tech Design Question 2 | Design adds new `archiveEntries` while bridging current history for compatibility. No historical migration/backfill is included. | Resolved - clarified |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:39:| Finalization boundary must prevent raw deltas and interrupted partial objects | AC-2.x, Tech Design Question 3 | Design introduces `ArchiveFinalizationService` and `finalizationKey` idempotency. Only completed objects call append. | Resolved |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:40:| Turn and derived-view persistence could accidentally become canonical truth | AC-4.x, AC-5.x | Design treats turns and derived views as cached/rebuildable projections over `archiveEntries`. | Resolved |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:53:| 1 | What durable schema stores archive entries, sequence numbers, related references, and idempotency keys? | Add `archiveEntries` with `projectId`, `processId`, `entryKind`, `sequence`, `finalizationKey`, `sourceObjectId`, body fields, related ids, status, and timestamps. Convex assigns sequence inside an append mutation and enforces `finalizationKey` idempotency per process. |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:55:| 3 | What finalization boundary determines when entries are archived? | `ArchiveFinalizationService` is called only from completion points: accepted user responses, completed model/runtime objects, completed script emissions, finalized tool calls/results, and process events. Raw live deltas and interrupted partial objects never call append. |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:57:| 5 | Should turns be persisted, computed on read, or cached with rebuild? | Turns are cached derived records in `archiveTurns` for bounded reads, but they are rebuildable from `archiveEntries` and never canonical truth. |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:58:| 6 | What minimal derived-view representation should Epic 7 implement? | Implement structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` views with source turn/archive ids, optional labels, and status metadata. No model-generated summaries or summarization prompts. |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:60:| 8 | What pagination/indexing keeps reads bounded? | Convex indexes `archiveEntries` by `processId, sequence`, `archiveTurns` by `processId, turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:61:| 9 | What idempotency strategy prevents duplicate archive entries? | `appendArchiveEntry` checks `processId + finalizationKey`. A replay returns the existing entry or no-ops. Sequence assignment happens only on first append. |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:108:    FINAL[ArchiveFinalizationService]\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:111:    READ[ArchiveReadService]\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:112:    DERIVE[TurnDerivationService]\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:113:    VIEWS[DerivedArchiveViewService]\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:129:`ArchiveFinalizationService` when a process object is complete. The service\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:133:The read path is broader. Fastify routes call `ArchiveReadService` for archive\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:134:entries, `TurnDerivationService` for turns, and `DerivedArchiveViewService` for\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:143:| Add new `archiveEntries` instead of replacing `processHistoryItems` | Current history is presentation-oriented and already used by live process surfaces | Epic 7 can preserve archive truth without destabilizing current UI |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:146:| Turns are cached projections | Long processes need bounded turn reads, but turns are derived | `archiveTurns` can be rebuilt from `archiveEntries` |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:157:├── archiveEntries.ts                         # NEW: append/read canonical archive entries\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:158:├── archiveTurns.ts                           # NEW: cached derived turn records\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:15