ory, full tech design, and test plan; inspected the new archive finalization service plus response/environment hooks and live-separation surfaces; ran focused story tests and the story gate; and reproduced a compatibility-bridge edge case in the real in-memory production path.\\\",\\\"priorFindingStatuses\\\":[],\\\"newFindings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"story2-user-message-bridge-key-mismatch\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Bridge-first user responses still create duplicate canonical archive entries\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"`ProcessHistoryCompatService` derives bridged `user_message` keys from `historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:61-68`), while `ProcessResponseService` archives the same accepted response under `response:${clientRequestId}` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:153-168`). `ArchiveFinalizationService` only short-circuits when an existing row with the same `sourceObjectId` is already present (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:70-79`), so the opposite order still duplicates. I reproduced this with `corepack pnpm exec tsx` by calling `submitProcessResponse()` -> `appendFromProcessHistoryItem()` -> `respond()`; the archive then contained two `user_message` rows for the same `sourceObjectId`: `response:process-archive-finalization:history-response-1` and `response:req-archive-4`.\\\",\\\"affectedFiles\\\":[\\\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\\\",\\\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts\\\",\\\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\\\",\\\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\\\"],\\\"requirementIds\\\":[\\\"AC-2.3\\\",\\\"TC-2.3b\\\",\\\"DoD-compatibility-mapping\\\"],\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\":\\\"quick-fix\\\",\\\"blocking\\\":true},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"story2-green-verify-format-failure\\\",\\\"severity\\\":