{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories compose into the intended archive -> turns -> structural views flow, and the full epic gate passed, but the durable Convex archive primitives bypass the Fastify access layer. That cross-story issue undermines archive read security, canonical archive integrity, turn cache integrity, and derived-view provenance.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The tech design says Fastify routes enforce project/process access before archive services run, and Convex should be durable append/read storage behind PlatformStore. In implementation, `convex/archiveEntries.ts` and `convex/archiveTurns.ts` register public Convex functions for sensitive archive reads/writes, while `ConvexPlatformStore` calls those public references directly. This creates a second production API path outside the designed Fastify/auth boundary.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Functional coverage is broad: canonical entry schema/taxonomy, idempotent append, bounded archive reads, finalization from process responses and environment execution results, turn derivation, structural derived views, provenance enrichment, degraded states, client surfaces, and e2e runtime rendering are implemented and covered by tests.\",\"Coverage is not acceptable for release because AC-3.3/A6 access boundaries are only enforced on Fastify routes, not on the public Convex functions that read and mutate the same archive data.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No material fake adapter, shim, or placeholder branch was found on the default production Fastify archive route path; `createApp` rejects `NullPlatformStore` in production and wires `ConvexPlatformStore` when live Convex config exists.\",\"Material non-real/bypass path found: archive and turn persistence are exposed through public Convex `query`/`mutation` registrations, so callers can read or mutate canonical archive/turn data without the real Fastify process-access production path.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"epic7-public-convex-archive-bypass\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Public Convex archive functions bypass project/process access and allow archive mutation\",\"evidence\":\"`convex/archiveEntries.ts:94-148` registers `appendArchiveEntry` as a public `mutation`, `convex/archiveEntries.ts:150-180` registers `listArchiveEntries` as a public `query`, and `convex/archiveEntries.ts:182-226` registers `patchArchiveEntry` as a public `mutation`. `convex/archiveTurns.ts:45-94` and `convex/archiveTurns.ts:96-124` likewise expose public turn cache write/read functions. These functions take only process/project ids and do not authenticate an actor or assert project/process access. `apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:788-828` and `apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2000-2035` show the production store targeting these public references directly. This bypasses the Fastify archive routes that do enforce access and violates AC-3.3/A6/security requirements.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"convex/archiveEntries.ts\",\"convex/archiveTurns.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.3a\",\"A6\",\"Security NFR\",\"Architecture: Fastify owns archive routes/access\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"epic7-derived-view-offset-pagination\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Derived-view Convex pagination uses offset-style cursor and can over-read for large cursors\",\"evidence\":\"`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:406-419` accepts any digit-only cursor, and `convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts:192-201` reads `args.limit + decodedCursor + 1` rows before slicing. A large authenticated cursor can force excessive reads or errors. Archive and turn reads use indexed greater-than cursors; derived views should follow the same bounded pattern or validate cursor range/shape more tightly.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-7.3\",\"Performance NFR\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
