ropriately doesn't handle the 409 conflict error since that's only for the refresh endpoint. The authentication checks also look right—unauthenticated requests get a 401 on API routes while the shell route redirects to login.\n\nThe `NullPlatformStore` implementation I noticed uses a fixed archive entry ID, but that's just a test stub, not production code. The real implementation goes through `ConvexPlatformStore` which properly calls the Convex mutation. Now I need to trace how the services are actually wired up to the Fastify app.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4077,"cache_read_input_tokens":85837,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4077},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ceb8cd2b-35ba-478c-a9f5-82f59e9dd21d","uuid":"cfdb2c9e-d11b-4c24-8139-dfb6b838449b"}
