ildTurns upserting by stable turnId.\",\n    \"AC-5.x covered by DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService producing turn_range and chunk_candidate views with structural labels only, plus refresh-time archive-signature checks that surface ARCHIVE_DERIVATION_CONFLICT when the archive moves under refresh.\",\n    \"AC-6.x covered by archive-entry-enrichment.ts which enriches relatedArtifactVersionId/relatedSourceProvenanceId at read time and degrades the affected entry rather than the whole page when lookups fail.\",\n    \"AC-7.x covered by durable Convex storage, cache-first turn/derived-view reads with lazy rebuild, and bounded page contracts (archive default 100/max 200, turns default 50/max 100, derived views default/max 50).\"\n  ],\n  \"productionPathFindings\": [\n    \"The default integrated execution payload at apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts emits archiveEntries: [] and a single process_event history item per run. As a result, the production runtime currently writes only user_message (via process-response.service.ts) and process_event (bridged via appendFromProcessHistoryItem) into canonical archive truth. The other five PRD-mandated kinds (model_message, reasoning, script_emission, tool_call, tool_result) are accepted by the Convex primitive and exercised by tests/fixtures but are not produced by any production code path. This was explicitly accepted by the user as platform-standup state per docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md and is not an Epic 7 scope violation, but it should be tracked when downstream model-driven runtimes are built so canonical archive content reflects real interactions rather than templated runtime briefs.\",\n    \"buildIntegratedWorkspaceExecutionSource in script-execution.service.ts is a templated process-type-keyed runtime that writes a static 'Process Runtime Brief' to disk and stages a static source note. It is not a fake adapter (real files written, real checkpoint candidates produced, real provider adapters execute it) but the synthesis content is hard-coded rather than model-generated. The intent is documented in the source ('default payload may produce runtime artifacts/checkpoint candidates, but it must not synthesize canonical archive entries') and the team-impl-log records this as accepted closeout state. No fix needed for Epic 7; surfacing for awareness.\",\n    \"InMemoryPlatformStore, InMemoryProviderAdapter, and FailingProviderAdapter exist only behind explicit test seams (options.platformStore, options.providerAdapter); production wiring in apps/platform/server/app.ts uses ConvexPlatformStore with LocalProviderAdapter and DaytonaProviderAdapter and rejects NullPlatformStore when NODE_ENV or LIMINAL_VITE_RUNTIME_MODE is production. No fake adapter is reachable on the production path.\",\n    \"tests/e2e/archive-runtime-flow.spec.ts boots a real Fastify server with real archive routes/services and exercises the browser via Playwright, but uses InMemoryPlatformStore with pre-populated archive/turn/view fixtures rather than booting Convex. The test:e2e gate is genuine (Playwright runs against a live HTTP server), not scaffold, but it does not provide a durable-store round-trip proof. Acceptable for Epic 7 closeout; convex/archiveEntries.test.ts and the service/server suites cover durable behavior against the Convex test harness.\",\n    \"convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts listDerivedArchiveViews uses an offset-encoded cursor scheme that reads .take(limit + decodedCursor + 1) on each call, so paginated reads are O(p**2) over page index p. Total derived views per process are structurally bounded (roughly 1.5x turn count) and the route caps limit at 50, so this is non-blocking, but it is a known scaling shape worth tracking if process sizes grow.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockingFindings\": [],\n  \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"epic7-archive-runtime-vocabulary-gap\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Production runtime emits only two of the seven canonical archive entry kinds\",\n      \"evidence\": \"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:253 sets archiveEntries: [] in the integrated default payload. apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:717-734 bridges process_event from history items, and apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:151 archives accepted user responses. There is no production caller that emits model_message, reasoning, script_emission, tool_call, or tool_result. team-impl-log.md records this as accepted platform-standup state at user direction.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\",\n        \"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\n        \"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-1.2\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"epic7-default-execution-payload-templated\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Default integrated execution payload is a static template rather than a model-driven runtime\",\n      \"evidence\": \"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:20-296 builds buildIntegratedWorkspaceExecutionSource using a runtimeProfileByProcessType lookup that hard-codes artifact title, source note title, history text, and commit message per process type. Real files are written and real checkpoint candidates are produced, but the synthesis content is not produced by a model.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"epic7-asymmetric-convex-apikey-gating\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"archiveEntries and archiveTurns mutations are exposed without the apiKey gate that derivedArchiveViews uses\",\n      \"evidence\": \"convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts:91-185 splits writes/reads into apiKey-checked *ForService wrappers and internal* handlers (Story 5 quick-fix). convex/archiveEntries.ts:94, :150, :182 and convex/archiveTurns.ts:45, :96 expose appendArchiveEntry, listArchiveEntries, patchArchiveEntry, upsertArchiveTurns, and listArchiveTurns as raw mutation/query without the same gate. Other repo tables (processes.ts, processOutputs.ts, sourceProvenance.ts) follow the same un-gated pattern, so this is consistent with repo convention but inconsistent with the Story 5 hardening pattern.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"convex/archiveEntries.ts\",\n        \"convex/archiveTurns.ts\",\n        \"convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"epic7-derived-view-pagination-offset-shape\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"Derived-view list pagination re-reads the prefix on every page\",\n      \"evidence\": \"convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts:188-216 listDerivedArchiveViews decodes a numeric offset cursor and calls .take(args.limit + decodedCursor + 1), then slices. Page N therefore loads N*limit rows server-side. Total derived views per process are structurally bounded (~1.5x turn count) and limit is capped at 50, so this stays bounded for realistic process sizes but is O(p**2) over page index.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-7.3\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"epic7-e2e-uses-in-memory-store\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Archive E2E test runs against InMemoryPlatformStore with pre-populated fixtures rather than Convex\",\n      \"evidence\": \"tests/e2e/archive-runtime-flow.spec.ts:67-86 constructs an InMemoryPlatformStore with archiveEntriesByProcessId, derivedArchiveViewsByProcessId pre-populated from fixtures and passes it via buildApp's platformStore option. Playwright then asserts on rendered DOM. This validates routing, shell, and UI rendering but does not exercise the real ConvexPlatformStore round-trip.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"tests/e2e/archive-runtime-flow.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/utils/build-app.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [],\n  \"gateResult\": \"not-run\"\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8366fdc4-8e5c-4246-9b1c-47fd55763cba","total_cost_usd":4.6915605,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":180274,"cache_read_input_tokens":5932086,"output_tokens":23888,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":180274,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":7049,"cache_read_input_tokens":196821,"cache_creation_input_tokens":170,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":170},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1310,"outputTokens":14,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00138,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-7[1m]":{"inputTokens":45,"outputTokens":23888,"cacheReadInputTokens":5932086,"cacheCreationInputTokens":180274,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":4.690180499999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"perm