{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01XkjtNHnSd2pD45BN7jFaw8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough evidence now. Let me produce the review output.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n  \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n    \"All eight stories flow correctly: archive primitives (Story 1) → finalization boundary (Story 2) → read/reopen surface (Story 3) → turn derivation (Story 4) → structural views (Story 5) → provenance coherence (Story 6) → reload/bounded-reads hardening (Story 7). No cross-story schema or ID drift found.\",\n    \"Turn derivation correctly uses stable `${processId}:turn:${turnIndex}` IDs; derived views reference those IDs as `sourceTurnIds`, so provenance stays valid across turn-cache rebuilds as the tech design requires.\",\n    \"Derived view IDs are deterministic (`${processId}:derived-view:${viewKind}:${startIndex}-${endIndex}`), which keeps provenance traceable after refresh without requiring opaque row IDs.\",\n    \"Cache invalidation on archive append deletes both archiveTurns and derivedArchiveViews atomically inside the Convex mutation, preventing stale cached projections from surviving a new entry.\",\n    \"Finalization boundary in process-environment.service.ts calls `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` for history-item-sourced entries and `appendFinalizedEntry` for runtime archive entries — the two paths remain distinct and do not cross-contaminate.\"\n  ],\n  \"architectureFindings\": [\n    \"Module layout matches the tech design file architecture exactly: convex/archiveEntries.ts, convex/archiveTurns.ts, convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts, convex/schema.ts, archive services, archive routes, archive contracts, and client sections are all present.\",\n    \"Service wiring in app.ts constructs DefaultArchiveReadService, DefaultTurnDerivationService, and DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService using platformStore, processAccessService, and sourceProvenanceService — exactly as the tech design specifies.\",\n    \"Fastify owns finalization policy and orchestration; Convex owns atomic sequence assignment, idempotency guard, and durable storage — consistent with the architecture split described in the design.\",\n    \"The `archiveFinalizationService` is injected into `ProcessEnvironmentService` and `ProcessResponseService` as a constructor default, meaning both services gain archive finalization without an explicit factory wiring step in app.ts. This is correct but differs slightly from the tech-design module matrix which implies explicit ownership — not a blocking issue.\",\n    \"`DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService.listViews` shares a lazy warm-up path with `getTurns` in `DefaultTurnDerivationService`. Both correctly fall back to `rebuildTurns` when the turn cache is empty, preserving the rebuildable-not-canonical contract.\",\n    \"`listAllArchiveEntries` is duplicated between turn-derivation.service.ts and derived-archive-view.service.ts. The implementations are identical. Not a functional problem but a minor cohesion gap relative to the module responsibility matrix.\"\n  ],\n  \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n    \"AC-1.x (finalized entry persistence, taxonomy, ordering, idempotency, related-id links): Fully covered. Convex appendArchiveEntry validates entry kinds via a Set, assigns sequence atomically by taking the highest existing sequence + 1, and returns early on a finalizationKey hit.\",\n    \"AC-2.x (live/archive separation): Covered by archiveFinalizationService.appendFromProcessHistoryItem (only for finalized lifecycleState) and appendFinalizedEntry (only called from completion hooks). Raw delta and interrupted partial paths do not call either method.\",\n    \"AC-3.x (archive read, reopen, access boundaries, degraded entry display): Covered. processAccessService.assertProcessAccess is called before every archive read. Empty and degraded states are returned through the archivePageSchema parse contract.\",\n    \"AC-4.x (turn derivation, immutability of archive entries, degraded turn handling): Covered. deriveTurnsFromArchiveEntries is deterministic over sorted entries. Degradation propagates from entries to turns without mutating archive rows.\",\n    \"AC-5.x (structural derived views without generated summaries): Covered. buildDerivedArchiveViews generates turn_range and chunk_candidate views. bodyText is set to a deterministic label string (e.g. 'Turn 0', 'Turns 0-1'). No model-generated content path exists.\",\n    \"AC-6.x (artifact and source provenance enrichment, per-entry degradation): Covered. enrichArchiveEntries batches artifact version lookups and source provenance lookups; each entry degrades independently when its related record is unavailable.\",\n    \"AC-7.x (reload/environment-loss survival, bounded reads, derived-view failure isolation): Covered. All reads are from Convex durable storage. Pagination limits are enforced. Archive reads succeed when derived-view refresh throws an AppError — the routes handle them independently.\",\n    \"All 41 named TCs map to existing test files (convex/archiveEntries.test.ts, tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts, archive-finalization.test.ts, turn-derivation.test.ts, derived-archive-view.test.ts, and client section tests). An additional `tests/service/client/archive-router.test.ts` tests the TC-7.2a canonical-archive-visible-during-view-failure path at the full client routing level — this test is not in the plan but extends coverage.\"\n  ],\n  \"productionPathFindings\": [\n    \"ConvexPlatformStore (production) uses real makeFunctionReference calls to Convex mutations and queries: appendArchiveEntry → archiveEntries:appendArchiveEntry, upsertArchiveTurns → archiveTurns:upsertArchiveTurns, replaceDerivedArchiveViews → derivedArchiveViews:replaceDerivedArchiveViewsForService, etc. No shims or fake adapters on the production path.\",\n    \"DefaultArchiveReadService, DefaultTurnDerivationService, and DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService are instantiated unconditionally in app.ts when not overridden via test options — the production path is always real.\",\n    \"NullPlatformStore and InMemoryPlatformStore are test doubles only. NullPlatformStore.appendArchiveEntry returns a hardcoded archiveEntryId (`${args.processId}:archive:0`) and listArchiveEntries returns empty — this is not reachable from any production route registration.\",\n    \"archiveFinalizationService is constructed with a default `new ArchiveFinalizationService(platformStore)` inside ProcessEnvironmentService and ProcessResponseService constructors. In production, platformStore is ConvexPlatformStore, so the archive finalization path is real.\",\n    \"No TODO, placeholder, or stub comments found in any archive service, Convex function, or route handler on the production code path.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockingFindings\": [],\n  \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NB-1\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"appendFinalizedEntry enforces sourceObjectId non-null for all entry kinds\",\n      \"evidence\": \"archive-finalization.service.ts:31-33 throws `Finalized ${args.entryKind} entries require a sourceObjectId.` for any null sourceObjectId. The spec contract marks sourceObjectId as optional (`no | non-empty when present`). If a runtime produces a reasoning or script_emission entry without a sourceObjectId, appendFinalizedEntry will throw rather than falling back to Convex's nullable schema.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-1.1\", \"AC-2.3\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NB-2\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"listAllArchiveEntries helper is duplicated across two service files\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An identical listAllArchiveEntries pagination loop appears in both turn-derivation.service.ts