{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Archive storage, archive reads, turn derivation, and derived-view reads are all wired together, and both `green-verify` and `verify-all` passed in this review.\",\"The epic still has a cross-story delivery gap: first-party runtime code only archives `user_message` and `process_event` directly, while the rest of the canonical taxonomy depends on externally supplied `RuntimeArchiveEntry[]` payloads that no checked-in production path emits.\",\"Deferred artifact/source reconciliation correctly invalidates cached turns/views, but the rebuild paths can repopulate those caches from a stale snapshot because derivation safeguards are incomplete.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The implementation matches the intended storage split: `archiveEntries` are canonical, while `archiveTurns` and `derivedArchiveViews` are rebuildable projections.\",\"It drifts from the tech design's finalization-boundary contract for model/tool/script outputs: Fastify stores whatever execution results hand it, but the platform does not itself normalize first-party model/tool/script completions into canonical archive rows.\",\"The derived-view conflict guard fingerprints only `archiveEntryId`, `sequence`, and `recordedAt`, so it ignores archive fields that actually affect turn grouping and degraded provenance.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"`corepack pnpm run green-verify` passed.\",\"`corepack pnpm run verify-all` passed.\",\"Coverage is strong for schema/store/service behavior, but the browser e2e archive test seeds archive state directly into `InMemoryPlatformStore` instead of exercising archive production from a real process execution path.\",\"Service tests for non-user archive kinds inject `RuntimeArchiveEntry` fixtures directly, so they do not prove that a checked-in production execution path emits `model_message`, `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result` rows.\",\"No automated test covers deferred archive patching racing with turn rebuild or derived-view refresh.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"When live Convex config exists, the archive path is real and the automated gates are green.\",\"Outside that configuration, `createApp` still falls back to `NullPlatformStore`, which synthesizes archive writes and returns empty archive/turn/view pages; this is a non-real execution path that can still boot outside production.\",\"The built-in default and failure execution paths emit `archiveEntries: []`, so canonical capture of `model_message`, `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, and `tool_result` is not real in the shipped runtime path unless a script manually supplies those payloads.\",\"Deferred provenance reconciliation patches canonical archive rows after append, and the current rebuild/refresh safeguards are not strong enough to guarantee turns/views always reflect that patched archive truth.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EPIC7-B001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Most canonical archive kinds still have no first-party production producer\",\"evidence\":\"`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:151-167` archives only `user_message`. The built-in default execution path returns `archiveEntries: []` in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:240-253`, and the built-in provider failure paths do the same in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/local-provider-adapter.ts:344-358` and `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/daytona-provider-adapter.ts:477-491`. The only built-in compatibility bridge in `apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:8-23` can map `user_message`, `process_message`, and `process_event`, but a repo-wide non-test search shows no checked-in producer for `process_message`, `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result`. In practice, most of the required taxonomy is only reachable if a script manually returns raw `RuntimeArchiveEntry[]` objects.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/local-provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/daytona-provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"TC-1.1b\",\"AC-1.2\",\"TC-1.2a\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EPIC7-B002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Turn and derived-view caches can be repopulated from stale archive state during deferred reconciliation\",\"evidence\":\"`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:54-67` reads archive entries, derives turns, and upserts them with no post-read archive-state check. Meanwhile deferred relation settlement patches archive rows later in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:795-829`, and both stores invalidate cached turns/views on patch (`convex/archiveEntries.ts:182-226`, `apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3325-3364`). `apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:126-165` tries to detect drift, but `computeArchiveSignature` at `apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:262-270` fingerprints only `archiveEntryId:sequence:recordedAt`, so patches to `relatedArtifactVersionId`, `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, `relatedToolCallId`, `entryStatus`, or `degradationReason` are invisible. A patch that lands between the initial read and the later upsert/replace can therefore leave stale turns or views persisted even though canonical archive truth changed.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"convex/archiveEntries.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-4.4\",\"AC-5.5\",\"AC-7.1\",\"AC-7.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EPIC7-N001\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"A placeholder archive stack still boots outside production when Convex is missing\",\"evidence\":\"`apps/platform/server/app.ts:190-227` defaults to `story0PlaceholderEnv` and `NullPlatformStore` whenever live Convex config is absent, only hard-failing when the runtime is explicitly production. On that path, `apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:1480-1535` synthesizes `appendArchiveEntry` responses but always returns empty archive, turn, and derived-view reads, and the same class returns placeholder process labels such as `Unavailable process` at `apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:1150-1184`. This is a deliberate non-real path, but it can still mask missing durable archive backing in local or staging environments.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"I did not run a manual live Convex-backed archive scenario; the producer-gap conclusion is based on the checked-in code and automated tests.\",\"If the team intentionally wants `NullPlatformStore` available outside production for story/demo bootstrapping, that policy should be made explicit so archive reviews can treat it as an allowed non-production exception.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
