outing and UI against InMemoryPlatformStore, not a real Convex durable-storage round-trip\",\n      \"evidence\": \"tests/e2e/archive-runtime-flow.spec.ts:67-86 constructs InMemoryPlatformStore with pre-populated archive/turn/view fixtures and passes it via buildApp's platformStore option. Playwright asserts on rendered DOM against a live Fastify server. This validates routing, shell, and UI rendering but does not exercise ConvexPlatformStore. Acceptable for Epic 7 closeout; convex/archiveEntries.test.ts and service suites cover durable behavior.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"tests/e2e/archive-runtime-flow.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/utils/build-app.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [\n    \"Whether the apiKey gate pattern from derivedArchiveViews (Story 5 hardening) should be propagated to archiveEntries and archiveTurns needs a human ruling. The current pattern is consistent with repo convention for other tables but asymmetric with the Story 5 fix. Resolution depends on whether the Convex deployment URL is treated as a private server-to-server boundary or as a potentially leakable surface.\",\n    \"Whether NullPlatformStore availability outside production is acceptable for local/staging bootstrapping or should be restricted to avoid masking missing Convex config. No code change warranted without a human policy decision.\",\n    \"If real model/tool producers are wired before a dedicated hardening story, CANON-N002 (archive signature gap) and CANON-N005 (appendFinalizedEntry sourceObjectId strictness) are the two items most likely to surface as observable runtime bugs at that time.\"\n  ],\n  \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2a93b29d-c885-4744-841e-e7896fb6b8e6","total_cost_usd":0.5702847,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":48936,"cache_read_input_tokens":191619,"output